imum aggression\n- White's knights, while advanced, don't defend f2\n\nReason: Qd8-h4 puts immediate tactical pressure on White by threatening Qxf2 checkmate. White's f2 pawn is only defended by the king, and this forcing move requires an immediate defensive response, potentially disrupting White's development advantage and giving Black time to catch up in development.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
