ut of check)\n4. Creates immediate winning threats\n\nReason: Q: h4-f2 delivers check and puts overwhelming pressure on White's exposed king. The f2 square is a classic weak point in the opening, and with White's king still in the center and underdeveloped pieces, this check will likely lead to a quick victory. White's options are very limited - the king must move (losing castling rights) or a piece must block, and in either case, Black maintains a winning advantage.\n\nAnswer: Q: h4-f2"}
